{{!-- The Ask tab, on a page that is not the Ask workspace.

     WHY THIS IS A DOOR AND NOT THE THING ITSELF. Ask stopped being a
     panel on 2026-09-14. It is a conversation with a history rail, a
     source pane and a composer that owns the viewport, which is not
     something that fits inside a tab alongside Power Search and the
     Desk. So the tab says what Ask is now and opens it.

     The old single-shot panel (_ask-panel.hbs) is still in the theme
     and still rendered by nothing: it is kept until the workspace has
     been exercised by real members, so reverting is a one-line change
     back to `{{> "faith-received/_ask-panel"}}` on the three pages that
     used it. --}}
<div class="faith-ask-door">
  <h2 class="faith-ask-door-title">A question, answered from the library itself.</h2>
  <p class="faith-ask-door-body">
    Nineteen thousand works of Christian theology are open in front of you.
    Every claim in the answer carries a citation you can open in the reader.
  </p>
  <p class="faith-ask-door-body">
    Ask now keeps your conversations, lets you follow a question through several
    turns, and opens each cited page beside the answer.
  </p>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/the-faith-received/ask/" data-feature-gate="ask">Open Ask</a>
</div>
